{
  "name": "cod",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-21, tools/creaturegen/rework/fish/cod.py): an Atlantic cod, 1 m -- a heavy body with a big head (a quarter of its length) and a pot belly; the upper jaw OVERHANGING the lower, a single fleshy BARBEL on the chin (a `horn`); THREE rounded dorsal fins and TWO anal fins, thin pelvics far forward under the throat, broad pectorals, a nearly SQUARE tail; olive-brown, densely mottled and speckled (the coat pattern `mottle`), a cream belly, and the PALE LATERAL LINE arching high over the pectoral, then running straight to the tail. Each fin is one membrane sheet. A SWIMMER (the fish's plumbing).",
